<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>South Sudan's road to elections remains uncertain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2f09c0afacb8321ae29dbd6f760cd125010a9c28556e0c41b65b3a4ea1a5a98</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442--6016ef79f3a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan's first general election is set for December 22. Insecurity, political tensions and failure to begin voter registration have raised doubts over whether the poll can be held credibly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The solar boom is rapidly transforming emerging economies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54b5ed33f6b7c6d836efb1773c3feb08ec8f9b25bc3ea2f9923fd98a221cd9c4</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-solar-boom-is-rapidly-transforming-emerging-economies/a-79474847--4010881b7e37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-solar-boom-is-rapidly-transforming-emerging-economies/a-79474847?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Renewable electricity is cheaper than ever. While the West got rich on coal and oil, some of the world's poorest countries are banking on solar, wind and water instead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Mali: Junta forces retake strategic town of Kidal from separatists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f5456c7cd8661fa75b97e0786b36d25dc9f2536d9c5acb577cb3dd465599ca5</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mali-junta-forces-retake-strategic-town-of-kidal-from-separatists/a-79570617--dc7ca7f76853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mali-junta-forces-retake-strategic-town-of-kidal-from-separatists/a-79570617?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mali's military regained control of the strategic town of Kidal after forcing Tuareg separatists and al Qaeda-linked jihadists to withdraw following an offensive backed by Russia's Africa Corps.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigerian military plane crash kills all 25 on board</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13ab9be7fa02216e0126f998efc7fd2301a3dbab15375c767f188e6fc152eba2</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigerian-military-plane-crash-kills-all-25-on-board/a-79552403--b7b9eaace4c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigerian-military-plane-crash-kills-all-25-on-board/a-79552403?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescue teams searched the crash site after the military aircraft went down in southern Nigeria, with everyone on board now confirmed to have died.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports first-ever Ebola death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fa08fd9e3b4de2357a73753abba87907eefbe270078467f1b8091e5a2496e5e</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death/a-79563120--66be6cae64d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death/a-79563120?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The patient arrived in Kenya over the weekend from the Democratic Republic of Congo before testing positive for the virus. Health authorities are on high alert and monitoring for more cases.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic report: Is Russia using AI for disinformation in the Central African Republic and elsewhere across Africa?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:735d473d877d87701f83407f108df0e63df8216b7eccc8c86cc6e55571ca4725</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T17:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-report-is-russia-using-ai-for-disinformation-in-the-central-african-republic-and-elsewhere/a-79476947--316a6e450389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-report-is-russia-using-ai-for-disinformation-in-the-central-african-republic-and-elsewhere-across-africa/a-79476947?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An Anthropic report says the AI model Claude was used in pro-Russian campaigns in the Central African Republic. Similar allegations were raised for the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya, Sudan and Mali.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco's first female head of government: Symbol or real reform?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:696bee2c524dcb5f8433da2441c55109e255a63e7f2f43ec1c863fd4a94b5790</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808--5c6131d5d637.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fatima Zahra Mansouri has been chosen as Morocco's first female prime minister. Is her appointment a kind of symbolism, to show Morocco in a positive light? Or could Mansouri bring genuine changes for Moroccan women?</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13c0e28f170b521025d902385c1de7834ff75decd575ef6505bf0df146298e65</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers for rejected asylum seekers outside the EU.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
